<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0020/e_0045/normalization> <http://digistrucmed.org/normalizationMappingMethod> "NONE" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0020/tu_0001> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "It is recommended that patients\\' literacy, cognitive status, psychologic state, culture, and access to social and financial resources be taken into account for optimal education and counseling. Because cognitive impairment and depression are common in HF and can seriously interfere with learning, patients should be screened for these. Appropriate interventions, such as supportive counseling and pharmacotherapy, are recommended for those patients found to be depressed. Patients found to be cognitively impaired need additional support to manage their HF. (Strength of Evidence = C)" .
